\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Mean IPCW integrated Brier scores across the primary Monte Carlo experiment, with Monte Carlo standard errors in parentheses. Means and Monte Carlo standard errors are computed over successful replications with finite metric values, out of 250 planned replications per scenario-method configuration. Lower values indicate better prediction over the common test-set evaluation horizon. This table includes all Poisson GG-KM kernel specifications, the Poisson spline, the promotion-time model, and the mixture-cure model. GG, P, Spl, PT, and Mix denote GG-KM, Poisson, spline, promotion time, and mixture cure, respectively; lin, RBF, lap, exp, cau, poly, and wav denote the linear, radial-basis, Laplacian, exponential, Cauchy, polynomial, and wavelet kernels. }}{8}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
